The figure illustrates how Nano-11 nanoparticles enhance the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) in vitro, as observed by flow cytometry. Panel A's dot plots show that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or Nano-11 alone are taken up to some extent, their co-incubation as a complex leads to a markedly increased co-localization and uptake of both the AF647-labeled Nano-11 and FITC-labeled OVA by BMDCs. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantifies this effect, showing a significant shift to higher fluorescence intensity for cells treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA alone, confirming Nano-11's role in enhancing antigen internalization.